{
  "case_id": "2007-06-11612",
  "document_hash": "859ff7dd0b50704aa1114a733541cada894e582dc3f2b7f64916d63ff1bc7b14",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11612",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "859ff7dd0b50704aa1114a733541cada894e582dc3f2b7f64916d63ff1bc7b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-859ff7dd0b50-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nBRENT E. NEWTON, ESQ., Assistant Federal Public\nDefender, Houston, Tex.; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nLISA S. BLATT, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General,\nDepartment of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of\nthe Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11612",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "859ff7dd0b50704aa1114a733541cada894e582dc3f2b7f64916d63ff1bc7b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-859ff7dd0b50-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. NEWTON: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice,\nand may it please the Court:\nPetitioner was not present at the bench\nconference and did not have the assistance of an\ninterpreter when the magistrate judge solicited his\nattorney's consent to conduct jury selection. The\nrecord does not reflect the Petitioner personally\nconsented or ever learned of his attorney's consent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11612",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "859ff7dd0b50704aa1114a733541cada894e582dc3f2b7f64916d63ff1bc7b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-859ff7dd0b50-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The record does not reflect the Petitioner personally consented or ever learned of his attorney's consent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11612",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "859ff7dd0b50704aa1114a733541cada894e582dc3f2b7f64916d63ff1bc7b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-859ff7dd0b50-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Newton, you're not\nclaiming in this case that the defendant was any way\ndisadvantaged by the magistrate judge conducting the\nvoir dire, are you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11612",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "859ff7dd0b50704aa1114a733541cada894e582dc3f2b7f64916d63ff1bc7b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-859ff7dd0b50-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Do you think there has to be a showing on the record that the waiver is knowing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11612",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "859ff7dd0b50704aa1114a733541cada894e582dc3f2b7f64916d63ff1bc7b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-859ff7dd0b50-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: I know it's a different context, but -- it does not relate to the magistrate versus Article III judge, but do you think that a lawyer could stipulate that the judge or a magistrate presiding could do all the questioning and the lawyers would do none, without the -- without the express consent of his client?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11612",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "859ff7dd0b50704aa1114a733541cada894e582dc3f2b7f64916d63ff1bc7b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-859ff7dd0b50-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The decision whether to have a magistrate judge conduct voir dire is a strategic call that counsel is uniquely qualified to make."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11612",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "859ff7dd0b50704aa1114a733541cada894e582dc3f2b7f64916d63ff1bc7b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-859ff7dd0b50-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Suppose -- I know you don't like to contemplate this, but that we accept the Petitioner's position that there has to be, that the client has to waive. Would we be better off just adopting the rule that there has to be express waiver, or would you then recommend that we ask the further question whether or not there was an implied consent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11612",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "859ff7dd0b50704aa1114a733541cada894e582dc3f2b7f64916d63ff1bc7b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-859ff7dd0b50-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could I just -- a question that has troubled me. Basically, what you say that is"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11612",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "859ff7dd0b50704aa1114a733541cada894e582dc3f2b7f64916d63ff1bc7b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-859ff7dd0b50-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'd like to return to Section 3401(b), which the plain language of, and the legislative history behind, clearly show a congressional intent in the -- context for personal waivers on the record by defendants. It would be anomalous not to require the same thing, at least in some similar form, in the felony context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11612",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "859ff7dd0b50704aa1114a733541cada894e582dc3f2b7f64916d63ff1bc7b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-859ff7dd0b50-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If there are no questions, we would ask that the Fifth Circuit's decision be affirmed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11612",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "859ff7dd0b50704aa1114a733541cada894e582dc3f2b7f64916d63ff1bc7b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-859ff7dd0b50-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government makes much of its claim that there could be meaningful Article III de novo review of magistrate judge rulings."
    },
    {
